  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-01-19T04:08:50.736Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I noticed that when you take a picture.. VRChat's virtual camera don't actually provided a lot of information that would be great to have. Use screenshots for examples and references.\n\nI understand it shows the date via the file name, but \"Date Taken\" (embedded into the file formation) is more important on the software side. When you transfer the file onto a phone, your phone isn't going to read the file name and put a date on it, its going to look for the date inside the file. But VRChat's camera does not provide this.\n\nI also think it would be really cool to include extra data if possible, like how when you take a picture in real life the image can get GPS data tied to it. For VRChat terms, it would be great to show what world the image was taken in, as well as the instance number. For the auther of the image, it should also be the username of the VRChat account taking the picture... and if possible for extra... \"authors\" included the usernames of users who where in the photo.",
